<title>USA: Digital expected to return to profit in Q2.</title>
<headline>Digital expected to return to profit in Q2.</headline>
<byline>Michael Ellis</byline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Digital Equipment Corp is expected to return to profitability in the second quarter as Chief Executive Robert Palmer predicted following the disastrous first quarter.</p>
<p>According to First Call, analysts expect second quarter earnings of about $0.10 per share, down from $0.91 a year ago, however their estimates range by a wide margin from a loss of $0.04 per share to a profit of $0.37.</p>
<p>Digital said it will post its results sometime around 0700 EST on Thursday and speak to analysts and the press later.</p>
</text>
